research/audit/wave0-judge-adjudications.jsonl:{"id":"ex-integers-mod-n-additive-group","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"c4138237518284d863e810a1d4e60a164d7a56da6b0e6b22428274112b6ee450","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"dependency_citation","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5, high reasoning effort)","at":"2026-08-02","note":"CONFIRMED FATAL and repaired. Step 3.1 asserts 'the elements of the natural number n being exactly the naturals s < n' with tags [step 2.2, step 1.4, L2, L5], and I verified that neither fact states it and that lem-nat-order-is-membership - the published theorem that does state it ('n = {m in N : m < n} for every n') - appears NOWHERE in this item, deps included. It is load-bearing: surjectivity of phi, and hence claim 3's |Z/n| = n, rests on the domain n being exactly {s : s < n}. Decisive aggravating evidence: the cited def-nat-order explicitly DISCLAIMS the property ('That coincidence is not proved here; it is derived from the additive definition above on a later page'), and two sibling items in this same wave cite the lemma correctly for the identical phrase, so this item is the outlier. Repair is additive paperwork: lem-nat-order-is-membership added to deps and to [L2], and tagged at step 3.1."}
research/audit/wave0-judge-adjudications.jsonl:{"id":"thm-reals-dedekind-field","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"8acf2bc01afdd4a91e42e709d022ac067edf7ede3a8d7b4d07d9fc915b399068","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"dependency_citation","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5, high reasoning effort)","at":"2026-08-02","note":"CONFIRMED FATAL and repaired. [L7] attributes 'products of positives are positive' to thm-rat-field, whose Statement has NO order content at all ('a field: a commutative ring with 1 != 0 in which every nonzero element has a multiplicative inverse'). The correct source, thm-rat-ordered-field, was absent from this item's deps entirely, while the proof uses Q's order substantially at steps 1.1, 1.3, 2.1 and 5.1. This is misattribution to a wrong source plus a genuinely missing direct dependency, not the under-reporting of a correct source that I graded nonfatal elsewhere in this wave. Repair: [L7] split so the field clauses cite thm-rat-field and the order clauses cite thm-rat-ordered-field, which is added to deps."}
research/audit/wave0-judge-adjudications.jsonl:{"id":"lem-rat-cut-embeds","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"c47a46c9fce73f7b5fb60245b1ff5cff5508985bf46cfcc26a71fef7301f3d9d","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"dependency_citation","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5, high reasoning effort)","at":"2026-08-02","note":"CONFIRMED FATAL and repaired. I verified the arithmetic myself: [L5] asserted the positive-case product formula 'for A, B >= 0*', but at A = 0* = {q < 0} no a in A is positive, so the second set is empty and the formula yields {q <= 0}, which has greatest element 0, is therefore not a cut at all, and is not 0* = {q < 0}. def-cut-multiplication restricts the formula to A, B > 0* and its Remark EXPLICITLY disclaims the boundary ('deliberately not applied at the boundary ... where {q <= 0} would leave 0 as a greatest element and so fail to be a cut'). [L5] was also internally inconsistent, its very next clause giving A.B = 0* when A is 0*. A reader-visible Facts-block assertion that is literally false and contradicts its cited definition's explicit disclaimer is not a citation-fidelity compression, and the 30-second rule governs GAPS, not false assertions. Mitigation, recorded: no step applies the formula at 0* (1.6 and 1.7 are stated for p,q > 0 and step 2.2 routes the zero case through the sign rule), so no conclusion failed. Repair: >= 0* changed to > 0*."}
