{"id":"lem-subset-of-countable","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"7a7053c27fd82da406ff1b7be83d4c360f66ff0a825ef86ef6a9371007cb7b5f","item_sha256":"71c3379f59e53d89665af09a5b9a4c4c2b280909b9387b08d4c0754280b4cc2e","outcome":"false_positive","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"A cited fact does license it. [L6] states \"m <= n iff m is a subset of n ([[lem-nat-order-is-membership]])\" and the Given fixes 0 = the empty set, so 0 is a subset of e(0) and hence 0 <= e(0). DeepSeek's premise that no cited fact supplies the base is refuted by the item's own [L6]."}
{"id":"lem-power-laws","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"c048c2dd051d2a4164b87cf5215fcb78a6c6acac8659dbc41cd9e32be9d1b054","item_sha256":"7ca99b37d0f3bc7dc4e132da0aaa52f2f544a2312c61c7d71a30179eb0240a93","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"[L5]'s dichotomy is true and one line from what its own cited items give: lem-nat-embeds-int characterises the nonnegative integers as the image of iota, and totality of the order on Z (thm-int-ordered-ring) supplies \"m >= 0 or -m > 0\". def-integer-power writes that exact derivation out in its own \"Integer exponents\" paragraph. The order item is not declared here; the claim is not overstated."}
