{"id":"lem-rational-power-well-defined","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"ab9f8cdc4559dd92b2df52c5935479f631a3c0fc0039e51a7a3a45f262b879e2","item_sha256":"d97667908f968e61bd168dea0f89467958d2005e87daacb82b94165731e324a2","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"The identity x^{-k} = (x^k)^{-1} is def-integer-power's own negative-exponent clause and claim 2 of lem-power-laws; both are declared in deps and lem-power-laws is carried as [L2] in this very item. [L3]'s citation list names only lem-power-monotone and lem-of-inverse-positive. Citation incompleteness on a definitional identity."}
{"id":"thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"8f871da00b39e680869d7852d255072b00967dbcc935b45f6a6d93165874c4d8","item_sha256":"293c2f72f9c1912e5bfe0995000d0349306a6ee91a43c4c781f110a88035695e","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"|x|^2 = x^2 is one line from what the cited items do state: lem-of-abs-value gives |xy| = |x||y| and |x| >= 0, so |x|^2 = |x.x| = |x^2| = x^2 since a square is nonnegative ([L2] of this item). The Fact bundles that consequence with its source rather than deriving it."}
{"id":"fs-rational-power-of-negative-base","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"ab75c642af675b82d4d50c9d515d3f581d8c652c0eadb2816d7f0df492af29d6","item_sha256":"ec73d2dce49d6db4fca3e91254ea1501103e6786b459ad539b120d5c8a98c208","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"The inference \"x >= 0 would give x^3 >= 0, hence x < 0\" is trichotomy in an ordered field. def-ordered-field is declared in deps and cited in [A1] of this same Facts block for exactly this kind of passage. [A4]'s citation list omits it; the argument is written out in full in the text."}
{"id":"cex-the-box-topology-disconnects-a-product-of-connected-spaces","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"0fb6d952d0ca5ed41c3eb3f0abd9fd315647e9b7ff658aa8c73187dad7a50b49","item_sha256":"0cd6140a375268b2d012431780caa17e6342623c890724dd83ef223fa208490e","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"The second clause of [A6] follows from the first in one step: given M, if M <= 0 then 1 > M, and if M > 0 then cor-archimedean-reciprocal at epsilon = 1/M gives k with 1/k < 1/M, hence k > M. The corollary is declared in deps and cited on the same line. A consequence bundled into a Fact rather than derived."}

