 ### Remaining blocker and exact next action
 
 A6 is mathematically complete but cannot honestly hand off to A7 until an independent current-text reader certifies the two UCL-host repairs and the orchestrator performs the required personal audit of the eight twice-touched source items. The exact next action is to rerun `--role certifier` on `source-ucl-closed-graph-pair`; on two `CERTIFIED` blocks matching hashes `0f9e69920fe94da65bcf3e7dfc0627f6b1394c0c84d94bfc124ab3a304e52961` and `e89824b7806d80bf48d312a69eb58d2251bc82c5b4e9080e2bcd6fe1c9293938`, write only their delegated verification stamps and update `wave6-published-repairs.md`. Then the orchestrator personally audits the eight-item escalation set, reruns `gates.mjs --audit --step A6 --run wave6`, and only then starts A7. No shell-permission prompt is permitted or needed for that handoff.
+
+## Recovery receipt — A8 adjudication (2026-08-08T10:31:00Z)
+
+- **Baseline and active stage verified:** `HEAD` is `84c52d136b16758747e7283118420cf88009148d`; the inherited dirty/untracked workspace was inspected and is being preserved. `research/audit/wave6-run-state.json` records A2, A3, A4, A6, and A7 complete and A8 active. The orchestrator's `pre-a8` stage snapshot exists at `2026-08-08T10:22:19.279Z`; its touch-ledger SHA-256 is `292c439efd616f3a8f847d4f0e8e643c4838aaaccdf349e235c760a59d07d383`.
+- **Normative and durable record recovered before A8 action:** `CLAUDE.md`, `AUDIT-WORKFLOW.md`, `README.md`, `SCHEMA.md`, `QUALITY-CONTROLS.md`, `briefs/audit-alpha.md`, `research/audit/RESUME.md`, this full Alpha report, `wave6-A0.md`, `wave6-A3-alpha-concurrence-task.md`, `wave6-A3.md`, all three Wave 6 findings files, all three provenance JSONL ledgers, `wave6-published-repairs.md`, and `wave6-run-state.json` were read in full or exhaustively parsed.
+- **Receipts and current scope recovered:** all three namespaced page manifests, `wave6-audit-manifest.json`, `wave6-split.json`, `wave6-batch-split.json`, all three namespaced proof-contract files and `wave6-proof-contracts.json`, `wave6-impact-template.json`, `wave6-impact.json`, `wave6-impact-audit.json`, `wave6-touches.json`, `wave6-url-liveness.json`, `genrisk.json`, `wave6-rejudge-targets.json`, `wave6-judge-attempts.jsonl`, and the complete 93-row `wave6-judge.jsonl` were read or exhaustively parsed. No `wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl` exists yet. The liveness table's three non-live rows already have the A6 dispositions recorded on disk: retain the official Padua timeout, remove the redundant dead MIT copy, and replace the legacy dead UCL host with its live official host.
+- **Mechanical receipts spot-checked:** the current audit manifest SHA-256 is `36ab80c78c1fa55c0d88a31e6fbf4fef04c1398408dc14d40bdc89d4003c3da1` with 1,393 rows (990 published-backward, 369 same-batch, 34 forward). The split is 121 pure / 5 material. The namespaced contracts contain 9 + 53 + 44 records and exactly match the 106-record merged contract. `wave6-impact.json` and `wave6-impact-audit.json` match at SHA-256 `709c009abfc606f82ff6b3b6cca825622e2c765d8615e630ae6d3051eaf40505`, covering 126 changed interfaces and all 912 consumers. `genrisk.json` has 80 seeds and the two targeted generated seeds retain concrete A6 dispositions.
+- **A7 scope and current hashes verified from disk:** `wave6-rejudge-targets.json` contains exactly 13 repaired ids. All 13 current normalized item hashes match the `pre-a8` snapshot. The exact current hashes of the four rejected items are `thm-laurent-cauchy-complete` `cc1b09d79aa5ca608eb9ca2a715999b9b4e104e152abd9fcda66a1d06dca64d0`; `cex-zero-times-infinity-indeterminate` `c8540f4b61482b0e72b08333b770ac6f4f747c66680519ecc5f909e1b3c40d36`; `cor-convex-subsets-of-rn-are-contractible` `bb1cce791779ab85da116f724147aed63a1b269df655dfd034a4fbe41580cf38`; and `lem-straight-line-homotopies-are-continuous` `4421293444a41a1cc2c640107442e57e67780346c1f2c43db34dfb0274765967`.
+- **Current-context rejection set:** the 26 targeted A7 rows are exactly 13 ids by two models. DeepSeek V4 Pro kept all 13; GPT 5.6 Terra rejected the four ids named above. The other 67 rows are preserved evidence from an obsolete stopped full-wave attempt and are outside `wave6-rejudge-targets.json`, so they will not be adjudicated or allowed to expand A8.
+- **Current mathematical surface read:** the four rejected item texts and each cited dependency implicated by the rejection were read from current disk, including the natural-order/induction chain, the extended-real/divergence definitions, and the convex-homotopy dependencies. The inherited open A8 action is to give each of the four current-context Terra rejections a fatal-only owner disposition, append one per-model/per-context ledger row with the present full normalized item hash, repair only any `confirmed_fatal` item, independently certify any Alpha-authored final text, and rejudge exactly the plain list of item ids whose own text changed.
