+  'thm-laurent-ordered-field': 'A4 added def-archimedean-field because the proof uses the canonical naturals being unbounded exactly through that definition; Audit-Alpha verified the new edge against both current items and the independent final-text reader certified it.',
+  'thm-laurent-cauchy-complete': 'A4 added thm-nat-linear-order to license the natural-index comparisons in the Cauchy argument; Audit-Alpha verified the exact statement, hypotheses, direction, and current proof use, and the independent final-text reader certified it.',
+  'cor-laurent-nested-intervals': 'A4 added thm-nat-linear-order to license monotonicity comparisons of the indexed endpoints; Audit-Alpha verified the exact statement, hypotheses, direction, and current proof use, and the independent final-text reader certified it.',
+};
+receipt.reviewer = 'Audit-Alpha wave 6 (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)';
+receipt.plan_reconciliation = receipt.plan_reconciliation.map((entry) => ({
+  ...entry,
+  reason: reasons[entry.id] ?? (() => { throw new Error(`missing reason for ${entry.id}`); })(),
+}));
+receipt.attestation = 'Audit-Alpha reconciled the complete current 126-item scope and all 1,393 declared relationships from disk: 1,166 logical edges through exact proof-contract citations, 180 other current body uses, 13 metadata-only dependencies, and 34 orientation-only forward references. Every high/critical item has a current independent DeepSeek V4 Pro reading and an Alpha risk disposition; every A4 or A6 repair has an independent final-text reading. The 13-item A7 repair target is exact, and the four current Terra rejections are hash-bound in wave6-judge-adjudications.jsonl as confirmed nonfatal under the owner thirty-second rule. No A8 item text changed.';
